  "id": "COMPOUND:41742 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Macrocarpal A and Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target interactions. Macrocarpal A is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including M-phase phosphoprotein 8, 4-methoxy-4-oxo-2-[(2-oxo-1H-quinoline-4-carbonyl)amino]butanoic acid, and Sorocenol G, all of which are implicated in targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C. These compounds are likely acting as modulators or inhibitors of Phosphodiesterase 6C, as indicated by their direct interaction with the enzyme. The consistent presence of Phosphodiesterase 6C as a target across these pathways suggests a possible functional or biochemical link between Macrocarpal A and the enzyme. The scores of 0.503 indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction. The evidence highlights the role of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 as a potential intermediary, though its exact function in this context remains to be determined.",
